Z||000003||FormulaJoe||12-23-2001||09:07 AM||||Your car have an automatic, I forget?  If it is an auto it could be the converter locking and unlocking.  I have an olds that does that at about that speed, drives me crazy. Only thing to do is avoid driving at that speed.  If you dont have an auto, well {in my best Gilda Radner voice} NEVERMIND!<BR>If you dont have an auto, check the things that the previous posts suggested.  Sounds like the car is bucking a little, that can be caused by several things. Vacuum leak, bad plug wires, etc.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
Z||000004||btoth||12-23-2001||12:54 PM||||My auto does that at around 40 and 25ish... feels like it's pulsating kinda.  And it's really noticable with the poly dogbone.  At ever other speed it's fine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smoooooth GT||12-23-2001||01:02 PM||||It's the TCC going out...   unplug it ... drive it.. and see if it still does it! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||California Kid||12-23-2001||01:03 PM||||Auto Trans will do that if the torque converter lock up sensor is malfunctioning. I believe there's a section in the Hayes Repair Manual that tells you how to check it out.||||reg||1
